SUMMARY:2025 TSC International Research Conference
LOCATION:Bethesda North Marriott Hotel & Conference Center\, Rockville\, Be
 thesda\, Maryland\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Biennial international research conference of the TSC Alliance\
 , subtitled 'Engage\, Accelerate\, Transform'\, bringing basic\, translati
 onal and clinical researchers together on tuberous sclerosis complex and t
 he overlapping disorders it touches: epilepsy\, autism and TSC-associated 
 neuropsychiatric disorders (TAND)\, lymphangioleiomyomatosis (LAM)\, renal
  disease and cancer. Four plenary sessions over three days\, plus mini-sym
 posia on TAND\, TSC disease mechanisms and genetics\, and LAM and angiomyo
 lipomas. The next edition is scheduled for 16–18 September 2027 at the s
 ame venue.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★★★): TSC is an mTOR disease 
 in the strictest sense: loss of the TSC1/TSC2 complex removes the brake on
  mTORC1\, and the resulting hyperactivation drives the tumours\, the epile
 psy and much of the neurological phenotype. The clinical use of rapalogs i
 n TSC is the closest the field comes to mTOR inhibition as licensed medici
 ne. Brendan Manning\, one of the five researchers the Atlas tracks most cl
 osely\, gave a plenary talk on 28 June titled 'Metabolic Effects of mTOR i
 n Tumors\, the Tumor Microenvironment\, and Host'. Mustafa Sahin (Boston C
 hildren's Hospital)\, whose TSC neurobiology work is in the corpus\, spoke
  in the TAND plenary on 'Investigating TAND and Epilepsy Using Human Neuro
 ns'. Several other talks name mTOR directly\, among them TREK1 inhibition 
 by mTOR and mTOR-LPL-driven lipid metabolism in TSC microglia.\n\nSpeakers
  or organisers with a profile in the Atlas: Brendan D. Manning\, Mustafa S
 ahin\n\nConference site: https://www.tscalliance.org/research-strategy/res
 earch-conferences/\n\nIn Oliver's mTOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/event
 s/#ev-2025-tsc-international-research-conference
URL:https://www.tscalliance.org/research-strategy/research-conferences/
